  "coordinate_frame": "Each mesh's vertices are already expressed in its MJCF body frame. Attach the loaded geometry to a group whose position/quaternion you set from MuJoCo FK body xpos/xquat, and apply NO extra local transform.",
  "notes": [
    "The MJCF geoms carry NO explicit pos/quat and NO meshscale; compiler is angle='radian' meshdir='assets'.",
    "IMPORTANT TRAP: MuJoCo's compiler recentres every mesh onto its inertial frame and stores the recovery transform in geom_pos/geom_quat, which compile to exactly mesh_pos/mesh_quat. Reading geom_pos/geom_quat out of the compiled MjModel and applying it to these raw STL files DOUBLE-APPLIES that transform and scrambles the arm. The correct local transform for these files is identity.",
    "Verified numerically: for a random joint configuration, world vertices from (body xpos/xquat) x (raw STL verts) match MuJoCo's own (geom_xpos/geom_xmat) x (compiled mesh_vert) to 7.4e-09 m, i.e. float32 STL rounding.",
    "Quaternions here are xyzw for three.js; MuJoCo's native order is wxyz.",
    "three.js is Y-up by default while this model is Z-up. Either set camera.up=(0,0,1) or rotate the whole robot root group by -90 deg about X; do it on the ROOT, never per link.",
    "The MJCF stands link_base on a 0.12 m pedestal (link_base pos='0 0 .12'). pi05/viz/fk.py subtracts that (MJCF_BASE_Z) to report FK in the xArm controller's flange frame. Whichever frame you draw in, use it for the base mesh too.",
    "link7's visual geom is end_tool.stl, not link7.stl. link7.stl is declared in the <asset> block of both xarm7.xml and xarm7_nohand.xml but is referenced by no geom, so it is not shipped.",
    "xarm7_nohand.xml has no gripper. Gripper meshes (base_link, left/right_finger, left/right_inner_knuckle, left/right_outer_knuckle) live in xarm7.xml and are not shipped here."
  ],
